### SkinMatch API - test with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or copy into Postman)
@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Catalogue (anyone)
GET {{base}}/products?category=serum&sort=price_asc

### 2. Filters: under 600 baht, for oily skin, treats acne (concern 1), no allergens
GET {{base}}/products?max_price=600&skin_type=oily&concern_id=1&exclude_allergens=1

### 3. Bad input -> 400
GET {{base}}/products?category=shampoo

### 4. Product page
GET {{base}}/products/1

### 5. Not logged in -> 401
GET {{base}}/me/profile

### 6. Log in as a member
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "member1@example.com", "password": "member1234" }

### 7. Wrong password -> 401 (same message as unknown email)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "member1@example.com", "password": "nope" }

### 8. My profile (id from the session)
GET {{base}}/me/profile

### 9. Save profile -> one transaction over 4 tables
PUT {{base}}/me/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "skin_type": "oily", "age_group": "18-24", "gender": "female", "skin_tone": "light",
  "concerns": [ { "concern_id": 1, "severity_level": 3 }, { "concern_id": 3, "severity_level": 2 } ],
  "allergens": [23] }

### 10. Unknown concern id -> transaction rolled back -> 400
PUT {{base}}/me/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{ "skin_type": "oily", "age_group": "18-24", "concerns": [ { "concern_id": 999 } ] }

### 11. Recommendations -> CALL sp_generate_recommendations
POST {{base}}/me/recommendations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "limit": 5 }

### 12. Review twice -> 409 (UNIQUE user_id, product_id)
POST {{base}}/products/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rating": 5, "comment": "again" }

### 13. A member calls an admin route -> 403
GET {{base}}/admin/report/brands

### 14. Log in as admin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo-admin@example.com", "password": "admin1234" }

### 15. Brand report (view v_brand_report)
GET {{base}}/admin/report/brands

### 16. Change a price -> trigger writes product_price_log
PATCH {{base}}/admin/products/13
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 470 }

### 17. Read the audit log
GET {{base}}/admin/price-log

### 18. Create a sunscreen (product + subtype + bridges in one transaction)
POST {{base}}/admin/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_name": "Test Sunscreen SPF30", "brand_id": 3, "category": "sunscreen", "price": 299, "volume_ml": 30,
  "gender_target": "unisex", "skin_types": ["oily", "normal"],
  "concerns": [ { "concern_id": 5, "effectiveness_level": 1 } ],
  "ingredients": [ { "ingredient_id": 15, "concentration_percent": 10 } ],
  "subtype": { "spf": 30, "pa_rating": "PA+++", "filter_type": "physical" } }

### 19. Log out
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
